 Local builds never publish or install a global CLI. Packaged Linux `orca-fork-build.json`
 and Mac `orca-local-build.json` record the full workbench HEAD; environment commit
-overrides cannot replace it. HarnessOS publication additionally requires the exact
-artifact's signing and bind qualifications. A local build alone is not qualification.
+overrides cannot replace it. Linux stamping also requires the verified build runner's
+`HOS_SERIES_DIGEST` and `HOS_BUILD_DIGEST` (64 lowercase hex each), recorded as
+`series` and `build`; absent or malformed values fail before writing a stamp.
+HarnessOS publication additionally requires the exact artifact's signing and bind
+qualifications. A local build alone is not qualification.
 
 Pi and OMP can share `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR`. Explicit agent launches install the
 same runtime-detecting status, prefill and titlebar templates into `agent/extensions/`;
